<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pforzheim</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pforzheim is a city at the northern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-forest">Black Forest</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It was a residence of the margraves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, and from 1767 it developed a major jewellery and watchmaking industry, earning the name 'Gold City'. Most of the city was destroyed in an air raid on 23 February 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pforzheim.jpg" alt="Pforzheim" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paralacre · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panorama_Nagold,_Stadtkirche_und_Enz_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
